#param float FPS 6 2 30 — poses per second: 12 is 24fps animation on twos, 6 on fours

// Stop Motion — 定格 · 抽帧. She moves ON TWOS: each pose held a few frames and
// then snapped to where she is now, the way limited animation and stop-motion
// move.
//
// An effect with no shader. What it changes is WHEN her pose reaches the
// screen, so it declares #stepped and the engine holds her skinning and her
// face between beats. Nothing underneath slows down — her motion and her
// physics run every frame, so each beat lands on the true pose for that moment
// and a held take never drifts off the music.
//
// Only the characters it is aimed at step. The stage, particles and every other
// effect stay smooth, which is what makes her read as animated rather than the
// playback as broken. Paused, nothing holds, so a pose edited on the timeline shows as
// it is edited. Put it on the timeline as a clip to step one passage.

